Given a Map<Integer, String>, write a Java program to count how many times each value occurs, including null.

We need to:
1. Iterate through all map values.
2. Count the frequency of each value.
3. Include null as a valid value.
4. Return a frequency map containing each distinct value and its count.
Example
Input:
Map<Integer, String> map = new HashMap<>();

map.put(1, "Java");
map.put(2, "Spring");
map.put(3, "Java");
map.put(4, null);
map.put(5, "Kafka");
map.put(6, null);
map.put(7, "Spring");
map.put(8, "Java");


Expected output:
Java   -> 3
Spring -> 2
Kafka  -> 1
null   -> 2

======

1. Recommended solution – Java 8 Streams using groupingBy()


import java.util.*;
import java.util.function.Function;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class CountDuplicateValues {

    public static Map<String, Long> countValues(
            Map<Integer, String> map) {

        if (map == null || map.isEmpty()) {
            return Collections.emptyMap();
        }

        return map.values()
                .stream()
                .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
                        Function.identity(),
                        HashMap::new,
                        Collectors.counting()
                ));
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Map<Integer, String> map = new HashMap<>();

        map.put(1, "Java");
        map.put(2, "Spring");
        map.put(3, "Java");
        map.put(4, null);
        map.put(5, "Kafka");
        map.put(6, null);
        map.put(7, "Spring");
        map.put(8, "Java");

        Map<String, Long> result = countValues(map);

        result.forEach((value, count) ->
                System.out.println(value + " -> " + count)
        );
    }
}
